{{Quote|The Forest Moon of Endor circles a gas giant in a system near the galactic frontier.|The ''[[Galactic Explorer's Guide]]''|<ref name="Galactic Explorer's Guide">''[[Star Wars: The Galactic Explorer's Guide]]''</ref>}}
'''Endor''', also called '''Tana''' by the [[Ewok]]s [[Homeworld|native]] to [[Endor|one]] of its [[moon]]s, was a [[gas giant]] located in the [[Endor system]],<ref name="TROS VD" /> a [[Binary star system|binary]]<ref name="Absolutely Everything You Need to Know" /> [[star system]] positioned in the [[Moddell sector]] of [[the galaxy]]'s [[Outer Rim Territories]]. Endor acted almost like a third sun to the moons with its clouds of hydrogen reflecting light.<ref name="TROS VD" /> Located in grid square H-16 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]], it was connected to [[Cerea]] and [[Bakura]] by a [[hyperspace route]].<ref name="Beginner Game" /> The [[planet]] was [[orbit]]ed by nine major moons,<ref name="TROS VD" /> the largest of which<ref name="Complete Locations">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> was known as the [[Endor|Forest Moon of Endor]]. The [[ocean]] moon of [[Kef Bir]] was also one of Endor's moons. Additionally, 48 "sub-lunar" objects [[orbit]]ed the planet.<ref name="TROS VD" />

Before the [[Hosnian Cataclysm|destruction]] of the [[New Republic]], the [[New Republic Senate|Galactic Senate]] attempted to rename the planet Tana, in honor of the Ewoks.<ref name="TROS VD" />

==Description==
Endor<ref name="TROS VD" />&mdash; known as Tana to the [[Ewok]]s of the [[planet]]'s [[Endor|Forest Moon]]<ref name="TROS VD" />&mdash; was a silver-banded [[gas giant]]<ref name="CLNE">''[[Star Wars: Complete Locations, New Edition]]''</ref> that [[orbit]]ed the [[Binary star system|binary]] [[star]]s of [[Endor I]] and [[Endor II]]<ref name="Absolutely Everything You Need to Know" /> in the [[Endor system]]<ref name="TROS VD" /> of the [[Moddell sector]],<ref name="TROS VD" /> a [[sector|subsector]] of the [[Outer Rim Territories]]' [[Zuma sector]]<ref name="Appendix" /> known for its notorious hyperspace anomalies.<ref name="TROS VD" /> Located at the edge of [[Lesser Space|known space]] and on the fringes of [[Galactic Frontier]]<ref name="CLNE">''[[Star Wars: Complete Locations, New Edition]]''</ref> in grid square H-16 of the [[Standard Galactic Grid]],<ref name="Beginner Game" /> Endor was located along the [[hyperspace route]]s of the [[Bakura Trace]], [[Ovise Reach]], and the [[Sanctuary Pipeline]].<ref name="BMF 18" />

A gas giant, Endor had no habitable surface, was 48,951 [[kilometer]]s (30,417 miles) in diameter, and had clouds of [[hydrogen]] in its atmosphere that reflected incoming sunlight onto its satellites, making it an effective<ref name="TROS VD" /> third<ref name="ThirdSun">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' states that Endor is an effective "second sun" for its moons; however ''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]'' establishes that the [[Endor system]] has two suns&mdash; [[Endor I]] and [[Endor II]]. As such, this article has adjusted the wording to reflect the Endor system's [[binary star system]] status.</ref> sun for Endor's life-supporting [[moon]]s. Endor was orbited by nine major moons: the [[forest|forested]] and largest moon of Endor IX3244-A "Forest Moon," the [[water|icy]] moon [[Korkar|IX3244-B]] "Korkar," the [[ocean]] moon [[Kef Bir|IX3244-C]] "Kef Bir," the crater-packed moon and possible captured [[comet]] [[Hual Maka|IX3244-D]] "Hual Maka," the rocky moon [[Sharls|IX3244-E]] "Sharls," the bleak moon with a [[nitrogen]]-rich atmosphere [[Vix|IX3244-F]] "Vix," the darkest moon of Endor [[Fentakka|IX3244-G]] "Fentakka," and the [[metal|metallic]] moon [[Alprezar|IX3244-H]] "Alprezar." Besides Endor's nine major moons, the planet was also orbited by forty-eight sub-lunar objects,<ref name="TROS VD" /> and after [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> a [[Death Star debris field|field]] of debris from the [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station]].<ref name="TROS VD" />

==Behind the scenes==
Endor was originally created for the [[1983]] film, [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']],<ref name="Return of the Jedi">{{Film|VI}}</ref> where it appeared as a distant orb, labeled "Planet Endor" by special effects storyboards, above its Forest Moon, not large enough to be definitively labeled a planet.<ref name="Endor">{{DB|location|endor|Endor}}</ref>

In the [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|rough draft]] and revised rough draft of the script for ''Return of the Jedi'', the [[Forest]] Moon of Endor, then known as the "Green Moon," instead orbited the [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[capital]] world of [[Had Abbadon system|Had Abbadon]],<ref name="annotated">''[[Star Wars: The Annotated Screenplays]]''</ref> which would later evolve into [[Coruscant]].<ref name="Coruscant">{{DB|location|coruscant|Coruscant}}</ref>

